{"id":"000VZ4","title":"Spoonful of Sugar","author":"NotSoMagnifique","solvedCount":4,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-10T02:12:53+00:00","posted":"Heute, 02:13 Uhr","rules":"My first Battenburg puzzle! As you might guess from the title, I started with the \"spoon\" configurations with the Battenburgs and the German Whispers, and then I filled in with some of my usual favorites.\n\n----\n\nRules:\n\n- Normal Sudoku rules apply.\n\n- Battenburg -Whenever 2 odd and 2 even digits form a 2x2 checkerboard pattern (e.g. R1C1 and R2C2 even, R1C2 and R2C1 odd), a Battenburg marking is given. If there is no such marking, the above pattern is not allowed.\n\n- German Whispers - neighboring digits on a green German Whisper line must differ in value by at least 5.\n\n- Renban - digits on a purple Renban line must form a consecutive set in some order.\n\n- Modular - each set of three digits along a teal modular line must have 1 digit from each of the following sets - (1,4,7), (2,5,8) and (3,6,9).\n\n- X pairs - digits separated by X sum to 10. No negative constraint.\n\n- Ratio Kropki - digits separated by a black Kropki dot have a 2:1 ratio. No negative constraint.\n\n----\n\nSudokupad\n\nPuzzle:","solutionCode":"Row 9 left to right","tags":["Sudoku","Kropki","XV (Variante)","Battenburg (Variante)","German Whispers (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/hxod5qogpq","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/hxod5qogpq","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-10T02:12:53+00:00"}